# 🚀 DevOps Lab — Real Incident Practice on AWS Kubernetes

> Built a production-like Kubernetes environment on AWS from scratch, simulated real P1 incidents, and resolved them using the same tools and process used by DevOps engineers in real companies.

---

## 🧱 What I Built

A fully functional DevOps practice lab on AWS consisting of:

- An **EC2 instance** (Ubuntu 22.04) on AWS free tier acting as a cloud server
- **Docker** installed and configured for container management
- **k3s** (lightweight Kubernetes) running as a single-node cluster
- A **production namespace** with a deployed login microservice
- **Prometheus + Grafana** for real-time monitoring and alerting
- A **GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline** that triggers on every git push

### Architecture

```
AWS EC2 (t2.micro — Ubuntu 22.04)
│
├── Docker (container runtime)
│
├── k3s (Kubernetes cluster)
│   ├── namespace: production
│   │   └── deployment: login-service (nginx:alpine)
│   └── namespace: monitoring
│       ├── Prometheus (metrics collection)
│       └── Grafana (dashboards + alerting)
│
└── GitHub Actions (CI/CD pipeline)
    └── triggers on push to main → build → deploy
```

