### Incident 3 — Server Disk Full

**Scenario:** Simulated disk filling up (common cause of DB write failures and app crashes in production).

**Investigation:**
```bash
# Checked overall disk usage
df -h

# Found which directories were consuming most space
du -sh /* 2>/dev/null | sort -rh | head -10

# Located large files
find / -size +100M -type f 2>/dev/null
```

**Fix:**
```bash
# Removed large dummy files
rm -f /tmp/bigfile

# Cleaned up unused Docker images and containers
docker system prune -f

# Cleared old system logs
sudo journalctl --vacuum-time=2d
```

**Result:** Recovered disk space. Learned that `docker system prune` alone can free 20–50GB on busy CI servers.

